{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "shape_ops_symbolic_subscripts",
    "description": "esm-spec 4.3.5: `index(reshape|transpose|concat(X), k...)` is an element of X at other subscripts, including when a subscript is an faq loop symbol. Each probe state integrates one constant gather out of a shape op, so its value at t = 1 is that element: v[i] = u[2,i] through a transpose, w[j] = a[j] through a reshape that inserts a unit axis, z[i] = a[i] + b[2] through a positional `broadcast` of a vector against a reshaped row, q[i] = c[i] through a concat whose joined-axis subscript is literal, and s = u[1,3] through an explicit perm. Every source array is held constant and every value is distinct, so a wrong axis order, a wrong element order or a wrong operand reads a different number.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST Test Suite"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "faq",
      "reshape",
      "transpose",
      "concat",
      "broadcast",
      "conformance",
      "esm-spec-4.3.5"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "shape_ops_symbolic_subscripts": {
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-09,
        "abs": 1e-12
      },
